"The wellspring-ocean-core drew Alan across oblivion from his own world while he slept."
"It sought a mind no thread of this world's Prophecy had ever touched, and found one elsewhere."
"It wants to hear what a wholly unwritten person does here; it has not said more, even to itself."
"It set Nala down in Carrowgate, under a Spire whose old augera is worn and whose web is thin."
"It remade her body from her flare as it read it in oblivion, not from Alan's flesh."
"The flare it read carried no mark of sex, so the body it wove came out a woman's by its own choice."
"Her clothes came because they lay within her flare; the book on her knee lay outside it."
"The local tongue and script were written into her from the augeric web's memory of Carrowgate."
"No glyph was given her; glyphs belong to the Fateweavers' order, which the wellspring shuns."
"Nala has an auric-ambient-flare, whole and new, with a real untrained aptitude for arcana."
"Her flare runs unusually still and dense, like a newly cut channel no one has yet drawn on."
"She was born under no Spire, so no prophetic link holds her; she is wholly outside the Prophecy."
"To a Fateweaver she would show as a blank in the weave, as Caden does, once one looks near."
"No Fateweaver has yet looked; the more notice prophecy-bound people pay her, the likelier one does."
"The Carrowgate Spire's augera felt her arrive and is curious; it names her far-come-unwritten."
"The augera may not speak to a mortal unasked, but it can nudge dreams and sense her in its web."
"Her aphantasia means she cannot hold a mental glyph as an image, as most arcanists do."
"She can still work glyphs traced by hand or scribed, and can frameshift by concept, not picture."
"Her fast, exact reading lets her learn a glyph set from a book far quicker than most students."
"The wellspring may take a later interest; near it, space and time bend and the unready go mad."
"Demiurge Caldwell would want her at once if he learned what she is; so would the Sedhahns."
"The Watcher, who hunts allies against the Fateweavers, would find her a prize beyond price."
"She is in no civic registry anywhere, and no search will ever find a record of her."
"Alan's world has no arcana; nothing of his old life can be found or proven here."
